🚕 Trips and Users — SQL
📌 Problem

Analyze the cancellation rate of taxi trips for each day while considering only trips where both the client and the driver are not banned.

The goal is to calculate the percentage of valid trips that were cancelled on each day.

Cancellation Types

A trip is considered cancelled when its status is:

cancelled_by_driver
cancelled_by_client
🗃️ Tables
Trips
Column	Description
id	Unique trip ID
client_id	ID of the client
driver_id	ID of the driver
city_id	ID of the city
status	Trip status
request_at	Date when the trip was requested
Users
Column	Description
users_id	Unique user ID
banned	Whether the user is banned
role	User role (client / driver)
🎯 Objective

Calculate the Cancellation Rate for each day from:

2013-10-01
2013-10-02
2013-10-03

Only trips involving non-banned clients and non-banned drivers should be included.

Formula
Cancellation Rate =
Cancelled Valid Trips / Total Valid Trips

The result should be rounded to 2 decimal places.

💡 Approach
Step 1 — Join the Users table twice

The Users table contains both clients and drivers, so we join it twice:

JOIN Users c
    ON t.client_id = c.users_id

JOIN Users d
    ON t.driver_id = d.users_id

Here:

c represents the client.
d represents the driver.
Step 2 — Remove banned users

Both the client and driver must be unbanned:

WHERE c.banned = 'No'
  AND d.banned = 'No'
Step 3 — Identify cancelled trips

Use CASE WHEN to count cancelled trips:

CASE
    WHEN status IN ('cancelled_by_driver', 'cancelled_by_client')
    THEN 1
    ELSE 0
END
Step 4 — Calculate the cancellation rate
Cancelled Trips / Total Valid Trips
Step 5 — Group the result by date
GROUP BY request_at
✅ SQL Solution
SELECT
    request_at AS Day,
    ROUND(
        SUM(
            CASE
                WHEN status IN ('cancelled_by_driver', 'cancelled_by_client')
                THEN 1
                ELSE 0
            END
        ) / COUNT(*),
        2
    ) AS `Cancellation Rate`
FROM Trips t
JOIN Users c
    ON t.client_id = c.users_id
JOIN Users d
    ON t.driver_id = d.users_id
WHERE c.banned = 'No'
  AND d.banned = 'No'
  AND request_at BETWEEN '2013-10-01' AND '2013-10-03'
GROUP BY request_at
ORDER BY request_at;
📊 Expected Output
Day	Cancellation Rate
2013-10-01	0.33
2013-10-02	0.00
2013-10-03	0.50
